From: Arch R
Subject: libretro: reject a state smaller than the core's own

retro_unserialize() had its size check commented out and copied a full
DoubleCherryGB state (megabytes) out of whatever it was given. RetroArch
keeps one save state folder per system, so a .state.auto left by
gambatte or mGBA for the same game (9.6 KB here) made it read past the
buffer: SIGSEGV in memcpy two seconds after the game opened. A state
smaller than retro_serialize_size() is now refused, RetroArch says the
--- a/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -626,7 +626,8 @@
 bool retro_unserialize(const void *data, size_t size)
 {
 
-    // if (size == retro_serialize_size())
+    /* A state from another Game Boy core is far smaller than ours. */
+    if (size >= retro_serialize_size())
     {
         unsigned i;
         uint8_t *ptr = (uint8_t *)data;
